->What is clean code?
    1. Reading it should make you smile the way a well crafted car would
    2. Elegant: No wasted cycles,
    3. Error handling,memory leaks, should be complete
    4. Clean code is focused, whereas bad code tries to do so many things
        Each function, class, modules exposes a single minded attitude that remains entirely undistracted, and unpolluted by surrounding fishes
    5. Good readability,high expressiveness
    6. Crisp abstraction
    7. Easy for other people than the original author to enhance it
    8. Code without tests is not clean at all        
    9. Smaller is better
    10. Clean code is code that has been taken care of
    11. Contains no duplication
        :When same thing is done over and over,its a sign that there is an idea in our mind that is not well represented in the code
        :Each module,function,class,object will tell itself hwo the next will be written

